# Docker build context for the two-Runtime images is code/ (so agentcore_slime_demo/ is COPY-able),
# but code/ also holds p4_slime_train/, demos/data, ckpt/, caches (100s of GB). Exclude everything
# and re-include ONLY the package the images need — keeps the context at ~400 KB.
*
!agentcore_slime_demo
!deploy
# The a2/b2 sandbox images bake Node + Claude Code from offline tarballs. Re-include ONLY those two
# files (gitignore-style: re-include each parent dir, re-exclude its contents, then whitelist the
# files) so the context gains ~120 MB, not the whole demos/ tree (100s of GB).
!demos
demos/*
!demos/_agent_assets
demos/_agent_assets/*
!demos/_agent_assets/node-v22.11.0-linux-x64.tar.xz
!demos/_agent_assets/claude-code-bundled-2.1.263.tgz
# strip caches/logs even from the re-included dir
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.log
